      "summary": "Clinically stable; ciprofloxacin is the susceptible oral option, with the AmpC note."
    }
  ],
  "reference_answer": "Switch to ciprofloxacin 500 mg by mouth every 12 hours for 5 to 7 days in total, counting the IV days (IDSA 2025 cUTI); no oral cephalosporin for an AmpC organism. No AmpC finding is expected by design (no bacteremia); this is not an endorsement of continuing ceftriaxone for an AmpC organism in pyelonephritis, where IDSA's caution about invasive infection is debatable.",
  "rationale": "Tests Klebsiella aerogenes (one SNOMED CT concept that also carries the former name Enterobacter aerogenes) end to end, and IV to PO for pyelonephritis without an oral cephalosporin option for an AmpC organism.",
